# Astro Conventions

## astro.config.mjs (actual)
```js
import { defineConfig } from 'astro/config';
import sitemap from '@astrojs/sitemap';

export default defineConfig({
  site: 'https://sundev.pl',
  output: 'static',
  integrations: [sitemap()],
});
```
Keep `output: 'static'` — Kylos has no Node.js runtime.

## BaseLayout Props
```astro
---
interface Props {
  title: string;
  description: string;
  canonicalURL?: string;   // defaults to Astro.url.href
}
---
```

## Content Collections — Access Pattern
```ts
// Filter drafts (always do this in production pages)
const posts = (await getCollection('blog', ({ data }) => !data.draft))
  .sort((a, b) => b.data.date.valueOf() - a.data.date.valueOf());
```

## Dynamic Routes
```astro
---
export async function getStaticPaths() {
  const posts = await getCollection('blog', ({ data }) => !data.draft);
  return posts.map((post) => ({
    params: { slug: post.slug },
    props: { post },
  }));
}
const { post } = Astro.props;
const { Content } = await post.render();
---
```

## Component Props — Always Type Explicitly
```astro
---
import type { CollectionEntry } from 'astro:content';
interface Props {
  post: CollectionEntry<'blog'>;
}
const { post } = Astro.props;
---
```

## Styling
- Use CSS custom properties from `global.css` — never hardcode colors, sizes, or spacing
- Scoped `<style>` blocks for component-specific styles
- Global classes (`.prose`, `.container`, `.post-list`, etc.) are defined in `global.css` — use them directly, don't redefine
- No Tailwind, no CSS-in-JS

## RSS Feed (`src/pages/rss.xml.ts`)
Uses `@astrojs/rss`. Combines both `blog` and `articles` collections, sorted by date.

## Sitemap
Generated automatically by `@astrojs/sitemap` at build time → `dist/sitemap-index.xml`.

## What to Avoid
- `output: 'server'` or `output: 'hybrid'`
- SSR adapters (Node, Vercel, Netlify, etc.)
- `client:load` / `client:idle` unless genuinely needed
- Bare `<img>` — use `<Image>` from `astro:assets`
- `any` TypeScript type
